,"props":{"className":"life-ad-rail","data-dock-active":"false","style":{"top":"94px"}},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-dock","hidden":true},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-ad-space life-ad-space-sponsored life-ad-space-compact","data-ad-placement":"ad_dock","data-ad-group":"reading","data-ad-creative":"read_product","data-ad-ready":"false","aria-label":"Advertisement · Community recommendation"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-ad-dismiss","aria-label":"Close ad"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-x","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 6 6 18"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 6 12 12"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-brand"},"children":[{"tag":"img","props":{"src":"/sites/howtolivebetter/images/shengcai/logo.png","width":"565","height":"144","alt":"Official Shengcai Youshu logo","decoding":"async"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-copy"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-label"},"children":["Advertisement · Community recommendation"]},{"tag":"strong","props":{},"children":["Could what you know become a useful product?"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["From ebooks to small tools, explore how members spot needs and turn knowledge into something people can use."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-actions"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-ad-space-link","href":"/en/shengcaiyoushu?sc_group=reading&sc_creative=read_product&sc_placement=ad_dock"},"children":["Explore the community and examples",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"18","height":"18","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M7 7h10v10"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M7 17 17 7"},"children":[]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"main","props":{"className":"life-reader life-tip-layout"},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-reader-sidebar life-tip-sidebar"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-back-link","href":"/en/book/10"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},"Back to index"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-sidebar-caption"},"children":["Is it worth dating and getting married?"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"data-ad-dock-host":"true"},"children":[]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"aria-label":"Chapter entries"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-01"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["01"]},"Getting to know more people rather than fixating on just one: You can’t predict compatibility before meeting someone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["02"]},"Stop after a clear refusal — continued pursuit is a public order violation, not “sincerity”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-03"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["03"]},"Judging whether someone is interested: focus on actions, not “signals” — who initiates, plans, and follows up"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Whether a relationship is good or not depends mainly on how you feel within it, not on your partner’s attributes"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"To build closeness, have two people take turns answering a series of progressively deeper questions — no script needed"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Long-distance relationships aren’t worse than local ones — the real challenge comes in the first three months after moving in together"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Check registration statistics before listening to elders: what do “marriage rate” and “divorce rate” actually mean?"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Accounting for the health benefits of marriage while adjusting for observational data"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Discussing labor division before marriage helps clarify unpaid work responsibilities"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"First check the default legal rules regarding marriage money and property, then decide whether to make a written agreement"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"When parents pay for a house, they should clearly state whether it’s a loan or a gift at the time of transfer"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Money borrowed by a spouse in a large amount — if you didn’t sign or later acknowledge it, it doesn’t automatically become your debt"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Obtaining a marriage certificate requires only an ID card and a signed declaration — no household register needed, no fees, and issuance is immediate"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Undergoing a premarital medical exam: if a serious illness is present, it must be disclosed before marriage registration"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Calculating the cost of walking away: Divorce by mutual agreement requires a 30-day cooling-off period, while divorce via litigation has strict legal prerequisites"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Make a separate tally for the benefits to your elders when they get married — don’t mix it with your own records"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Treating relationship quality as a health factor: focus on the issue, not the person — avoid insults and sarcasm"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"While both partners are of sound mind, complete power of attorney, designated guardianship, and wills: Legally, you are not close relatives; without these, you will have no signing authority or inheritance rights."]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Don’t marry while hiding your sexual orientation, and don’t treat “marriage of convenience” as an easy shortcut: legally, it is a real marriage, and the only way out is divorce"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/10-20","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"When a relationship is stuck in endless arguments and silent treatment, couples therapy can help — waiting alone rarely does"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/10"},"children":["Chapter 10"," ·"," ","Is it worth dating and getting married?"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"10-20"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["20"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a（争议）"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A（争议）"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["When a relationship is stuck in endless arguments and silent treatment, couples therapy can help — waiting alone rarely does"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Couples who attend therapy together tend to report significantly higher relationship satisfaction — roughly 70% experience noticeable improvement. In contrast, couples who simply wait without any intervention show little to no change. However, these benefits tend to fade over time: after five years, about half of those who sought therapy still report clear gains, while roughly a quarter end up separated or divorced."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Couples therapy comes at a cost. Fees are charged per sess…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A 2020 meta-analysis examined 58 studies involving 2,092 couples. After completing therapy, the average change…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: When a relationship is stuck in endless arguments and silent treatment, couples therapy can help — waiting alone rarely does"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Couples therapy comes at a cost. Fees are charged per session and vary by location and clinic; no exact figures are provided here. Typically, participants attend weekly sessions over a period of about eight months. The main challenge is that both partners must attend regularly and see it through to the end."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A 2020 meta-analysis examined 58 studies involving 2,092 couples. After completing therapy, the average change in relationship satisfaction was g = 1.12 (95% CI: 0.92–1.31), which researchers consider a large effect size. g is an effect size measure; see the glossary for details. For couples who only waited without therapy, the same period yielded g = 0.12 (−0.04 to 0.29), indicating virtually no improvement. The greater the initial dissatisfaction, the larger the subsequent gain. Another review from 2012 reported that 70% of couples receiving therapy showed positive outcomes. One randomized trial followed 134 long‑married couples with serious conflicts; after eight months of two different behavioral therapy programs, satisfaction improved by d = 0.90 and d = 0.71 respectively. Five years later, 50.0% and 45.9% of those couples still showed clinically meaningful improvement. At the same time, 25.7% and 27.9% had separated or divorced."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Roddy MK, Walsh LM, Rothman K, Hatch SG, Doss BD (2020). Meta-analysis of couple therapy: effects across outcomes, designs, timeframes, and other moderators. Journal of Consulting and Clinical Psychology, 88(7), 583-596. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/ccp0000514","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1037/ccp0000514"]},"；Lebow JL, Chambers AL, Christensen A, Johnson SM (2012). Research on the treatment of couple distress. Journal of Marital and Family Therapy, 38(1), 145-168. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1752-0606.2011.00249.x","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1752-0606.2011.00249.x"]},"；Christensen A, Atkins DC, Baucom B, Yi J (2010). Marital status and satisfaction five years following a randomized clinical trial comparing traditional versus integrative behavioral couple therapy. Journal of Consulting and Clinical Psychology, 78(2), 225-235. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/a0018132","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1037/a0018132"]},"；Rathgeber M, Bürkner PC, Schiller EM, Holling H (2019). The efficacy of emotionally focused couples therapy and behavioral couples therapy: a meta-analysis. Journal of Marital and Family Therapy, 45(3), 447-463. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jmft.12336","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1111/jmft.12336"]},"（争议方）；Shadish WR, Baldwin SA (2003). Meta-analysis of MFT interventions. Journal of Marital and Family Therapy, 29(4), 547-570. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1752-0606.2003.tb01694.x","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1752-0606.2003.tb01694.x"]},"（争议方）；Karakurt G, Whiting K, van Esch C, Bolen SD, Calabrese JR (2016). Couples therapy for intimate partner violence: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Journal of Marital and Family Therapy, 42(4), 567-583. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jmft.12178","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1111/jmft.12178"]},"；全国人大常委会 (2018 修正). 精神卫生法（第二十三、五十一条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=2c909fdd678bf17901678bf7448a066d","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=2c909fdd678bf17901678bf7448a066d"]},"（国家法律法规数据库）"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/ccp0000514","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["The main controversy concerns how long these benefits actually last. Another meta-analysis limited to randomized trials found g = 0.60 right after therapy and g = 0.44 after six months; by twelve months only one behavioral therapy approach retained any measurable effect, with g = 0.06 — essentially negligible. A broader review of 20 meta-analyses concluded that clinically meaningful improvement occurs in 40% to 50% of participants. The figures “70% improvement” and “40–50% clinically meaningful improvement” refer to different criteria and should not be directly compared. The five‑year trial lacked a control group of couples receiving no treatment, so it is unclear whether divorce rates rose or fell. The 2020 meta‑analysis included only heterosexual couples; no comparable randomized trials have been identified in China, so results should be interpreted with caution. In China, mental health regulations require that psychotherapy be delivered within medical institutions; counselors without medical qualifications may not provide psychotherapy. You can inquire at psychiatric or psychology departments of hospitals about available couples therapy programs. If seeking outside a hospital, verify the practitioner’s credentials and training. Couples experiencing domestic violence should not begin therapy together. A 2016 meta‑analysis noted that its conclusions apply only to mild‑to‑moderate conflicts where both partners occasionally engage in physical altercations; it does not cover situations dominated by controlling or severely harmful behavior. There is also concern that returning home after therapy might increase the risk of retaliation. If you have been physically abused, see Section 8, Item 43. For advice on how to talk during arguments, see Section 17; for guidance on whether to end the relationship, see Section 15. The primary beneficiaries of therapy are both you and your spouse."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/10-19"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Previous"]},"Don’t marry while hiding your sexual orientation, and don’t treat “marriage of convenience” as an easy shortcut: legally, it is a real marriage, and the only way out is divorce"]}]}]},{"tag":"section","props":{"className":"life-tip-related"},"children":[{"tag":"h2","props":{},"children":["More in this topic"]},{"tag":"ul","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-13"},"children":[{"tag":"strong","props":{},"children":["Obtaining a marriage certific